-- title:
--   Adic Galois representation from a Hecke character on J₁(M)
-- statement:
--   Let $M \geq 1$ and let $p$ be a prime. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation ring which is a domain, with a field $K$ realised as its fraction field, let $i_0 \colon \mathbb{Z}_p \to O$ be a ring homomorphism, and assume $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $O$. Equip $J = \mathrm{JOne}(M)$, the degree-zero divisor class group $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the function field of $X_1(M)$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, with the Hecke–diamond module structure [`ModularCurve.heckeModuleOneBar M`](def/ModularCurve_X1HeckeModule.html#L129), and let $A_1 =$ `rationalHeckeAlgebraOne` be the $\mathbb{Q}_p$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{Q}_p}(\mathbb{Q}_p \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_p} T_p J)$ generated by the images of the Hecke generators. Then for every ring homomorphism $\Lambda \colon A_1 \to K$ such that $\Lambda$ sends the image of each $c \in \mathbb{Z}_p \subseteq \mathbb{Q}_p$ to the image of $i_0(c)$ in $K$, there exists a [`GaloisRepAdic O`](def/GaloisRep_Adic.html#L16), that is an $O$-module $V$, free and finite of rank $2$, together with a monoid homomorphism $\rho$ from $\mathrm{Aut}_{\mathbb{Q}}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ to $\mathrm{End}_O(V)$ which is adically continuous (for each $n$ there is a finite extension $L/\mathbb{Q}$ inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ such that every $\sigma$ fixing $L$ pointwise satisfies $\rho(\sigma)v - v \in \mathfrak{m}_O^n V$ for all $v$), with the following two properties. First, for every prime $\ell \nmid Mp$ and all $a, d \in O$ with $\Lambda(T_\ell) = a$ and $\Lambda(\langle \ell \rangle) \cdot d = 1$ in $K$, for every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\ell$ a non-unit of $A$ and every $\sigma$ lying in the decomposition subgroup of $A$ and acting on the residue field of $A$ by $x \mapsto x^{\ell}$, the characteristic polynomial of the $O$-linear endomorphism $\rho(\sigma)$ is $X^2 - d a X + d \ell$. Second, for every prime $\ell \nmid Mp$, every valuation subring $A$ with $\ell$ a non-unit and every $\sigma$ in the image of the inertia subgroup of $A$, one has $\rho(\sigma) = 1$.
--
--   This is the Eichler–Shimura construction at level $\Gamma_1(M)$, in a coefficient-agnostic form: a $K$-valued character of the $p$-adic Hecke–diamond algebra acting on the Tate module of $J_1(M)$ produces a rank-two $O$-adic Galois representation with prescribed Frobenius characteristic polynomials away from $Mp$ and unramified outside $Mp$. It is the engine behind the attachment of Galois representations to Hecke eigenforms with nebentypus, used by [`CuspForm.IsEigenformWith.exists_galoisRepAdic_charpoly_frobenius_eq_and_isUnramifiedAt`](thm.html#CuspForm.IsEigenformWith.exists_galoisRepAdic_charpoly_frobenius_eq_and_isUnramifiedAt).
